  "published": "2026-11-07T01:39:37.883Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ExternalAuthResult gains FailureDetail, the provider package's own name for a refusal, set through a new four-parameter Failed overload; the existing Failed overload and ExternalAuthFailureReason are unchanged, so provider packages built against 5.13.1 run as before. HttpContext.SetNoStoreCacheControl() sets the Cache-Control: no-store every token-issuing endpoint sends. TimeProviderLifetimeValidator is now public, so a TokenValidationParameters built for another issuer's tokens can check lifetime on the registered clock. New ExternalSignInEndpoint.HandleAsync is the part every provider sign-in endpoint shares (no-store, the audit record, the access-token cookie, the progressive-delay reset, 200 or 401), with FindMissingServices for a provider's startup check, used by EasyReasy.Auth.Google 1.3.0 and EasyReasy.Auth.Microsoft 1.0.0. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-v5.14.0/EasyReasy.Auth/README.md#migration-from-5131",
